WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.876 --> 00:00:02.980
TOMORROW AFTERNOON.

00:00:02.982 --> 00:00:05.499
&gt;&gt; Sandra: THIS JUST IN.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.566
NEW WEEKLY JOBLESS NUMBERS

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:08.872
SHOWING 840,000 AMERICANS

00:00:08.874 --> 00:00:10.375
APPLIED FOR UNEMPLOYMENT

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:11.789
BENEFITS LAST WEEK ALONE.

00:00:11.823 --> 00:00:13.096
WHITE HOUSE ECONOMIC ADVISOR

00:00:13.097 --> 00:00:14.620
LARRY KUDLOW JOINS US NOW.

00:00:14.654 --> 00:00:16.627
GOOD MORNING TO YOU, LARRY.

00:00:16.628 --> 00:00:18.380
ALWAYS APPRECIATE YOUR TIME.

00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:20.936
WHAT DOES THIS NUMBER TELL YOU

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.235
ABOUT HOW THIS ECONOMIC

00:00:22.269 --> 00:00:23.630
RECOVERY IS GOING?

00:00:23.664 --> 00:00:25.638
BECAUSE THAT’S STILL -- THAT

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.907
NUMBER HOVERS AT AN HISTORIC

00:00:27.942 --> 00:00:29.749
HIGH FOR THIS COUNTRY.

00:00:29.751 --> 00:00:32.662
AS OF THIS MORNING, 29 WEEKS

00:00:32.664 --> 00:00:34.512
SINCE THE CORONAVIRUS LOCKDOWNS

00:00:34.547 --> 00:00:35.900
BEGAN THE NUMBER TOTALS 63

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:36.576
MILLION.

00:00:36.577 --> 00:00:38.934
THAT WORKS OUT TO 40% OF THE

00:00:38.935 --> 00:00:40.538
U.S. LABOR FORCE.

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:43.453
THIS IS A LOT OF AMERICANS

00:00:43.455 --> 00:00:45.504
STILL HURTING AS A RESULT OF

00:00:45.505 --> 00:00:46.341
THIS PANDEMIC.

00:00:46.342 --> 00:00:48.501
&gt;&gt; I DON’T DENY THAT A LOT OF

00:00:48.535 --> 00:00:49.842
AMERICANS ARE STILL HURTING.

00:00:49.877 --> 00:00:51.596
I THINK THERE IS STILL A LOT OF

00:00:51.597 --> 00:00:53.238
HARDSHIP OUT THERE.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:56.746
I DO WANT TO NOTE THESE WEEKLY

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.199
UNEMPLOYMENT CLAIMS HAVE FALLEN

00:00:58.233 --> 00:00:59.953
SHARPLY FROM THE PEAKS

00:00:59.954 --> 00:01:01.473
REGISTERED IN MID TO LATE

00:01:01.474 --> 00:01:02.270
APRIL, EARLY MAY.

00:01:02.305 --> 00:01:03.623
THEY HAVE BEEN TRENDING LOWER

00:01:03.624 --> 00:01:05.673
NOW FOR FIVE MONTHS.

00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:08.652
I ALSO WANT TO ADD TO THAT,

00:01:08.686 --> 00:01:10.773
SANDRA, CONTINUING CLAIMS WHICH

00:01:10.774 --> 00:01:13.616
IS THE ACTUAL PAYMENTS, NOT THE

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.499
APPLICATIONS BUT THE PAYMENTS

00:01:15.533 --> 00:01:18.008
FELL SHARPLY BY OVER 1 MILLION.

00:01:18.009 --> 00:01:21.567
THAT NUMBER IS USUALLY A PRETTY

00:01:21.568 --> 00:01:24.249
GOOD FORECASTER OF THE NEXT

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.645
MONTH’S JOB.

00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:27.813
SO I THINK LABOR SITUATION IS

00:01:27.848 --> 00:01:29.598
LOOKING MUCH BETTER.

00:01:29.599 --> 00:01:31.226
WE’RE MOVING IN THE RIGHT

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:31.878
DIRECTION.

00:01:31.913 --> 00:01:35.251
I MIGHT ADD 2/3 OF THE RETURN

00:01:35.286 --> 00:01:37.426
JOBS COME FROM THE LOWER WAGE

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.220
END SO WE’RE PROSPERING THERE.

00:01:39.221 --> 00:01:40.640
IT IS A TOUGH BATTLE.

00:01:40.674 --> 00:01:44.169
IT IS NOT GOING TO BE DONE JUST

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:45.583
IN FIVE MONTHS AFTER THE

00:01:45.617 --> 00:01:46.595
TERRIBLE PANDEMIC CONTRACTION

00:01:46.597 --> 00:01:48.516
AND ALL THAT WENT WITH IT.

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.934
THE REALITY IS THE ECONOMY IS

00:01:49.935 --> 00:01:52.034
IN THE RIGHT DIRECTION AND

00:01:52.068 --> 00:01:54.295
STILL LOOKS TO ME VERY MUCH

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.448
LIKE A V-SHAPED RECOVERY.

00:01:57.449 --> 00:02:00.654
YOU’LL HAVE A HUGE NUMBER FOR

00:02:00.655 --> 00:02:01.707
Q3 GDP.

00:02:01.708 --> 00:02:04.645
WE’VE BEEN SAYING 20% PLUS.

00:02:04.679 --> 00:02:07.539
THE FED AND OTHERS AND GOLDMAN

00:02:07.573 --> 00:02:09.688
SACHS SAYING 35%.

00:02:09.689 --> 00:02:11.530
HOUSING BOOM, AUTO BOOM,

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.860
RETAILING BOOM, MANUFACTURING

00:02:12.894 --> 00:02:16.479
BOOM GOING ON TO RESTOCK

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:17.089
INVENTORIES.

00:02:17.123 --> 00:02:21.133
WHEN YOU LOOK AT THE ALL THE

00:02:21.167 --> 00:02:22.898
NUMBERS YOU SEE A STRONG

00:02:22.899 --> 00:02:23.717
SELF-SUSTAINING RECOVERY.

00:02:23.718 --> 00:02:25.705
I STILL THINK WE SHOULD HAVE

00:02:25.739 --> 00:02:27.951
SOME OF THE TARGET ASSISTANCE

00:02:27.952 --> 00:02:29.942
PACKAGES THAT PRESIDENT TRUMP

00:02:29.976 --> 00:02:33.135
AND STEVE MUTSCHIN ARE TALKING

00:02:33.169 --> 00:02:34.166
ABOUT.

00:02:34.167 --> 00:02:37.411
THE ECONOMY IS IN HAVE GOOD

00:02:37.445 --> 00:02:39.633
FOOTING AND RECOVER EVERYTHING

00:02:39.635 --> 00:02:41.547
FASTER THAN ANYBODY THOUGHT.

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:42.917
EVEN THE FEDERAL RESERVE HAS

00:02:42.918 --> 00:02:44.030
UPPED ITS ECONOMIC GROWTH

00:02:44.032 --> 00:02:45.833
FORECAST FOR THE SECOND HALF OF

00:02:45.867 --> 00:02:47.321
THIS YEAR AND EARLY NEXT YEAR.

00:02:47.322 --> 00:02:49.853
&gt;&gt; Sandra: I WANT TO POINT OUT

00:02:49.854 --> 00:02:51.821
THE NEW CLAIMS ARE THE LOWEST,

00:02:51.822 --> 00:02:53.502
ALTHOUGH STILL VERY HIGH, THE

00:02:53.504 --> 00:02:55.189
LOWEST SINCE MARCH 14th.

00:02:55.191 --> 00:02:56.943
THE CONTINUING CLAIMS YOU POINT

00:02:56.945 --> 00:02:58.608
OUT, ANOTHER IMPORTANT NUMBER,

00:02:58.642 --> 00:03:01.131
ALMOST 11 MILLION BUT STILL THE

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.717
LOWEST SINCE MARCH 28th, LARRY.

00:03:02.751 --> 00:03:04.003
THE PRESIDENT JOINED MARIA

00:03:04.004 --> 00:03:05.904
BARTIROMO ON FOX BUSINESS AND

00:03:05.905 --> 00:03:07.605
ASKED WHY HE ENDED THOSE

00:03:07.607 --> 00:03:09.381
STIMULUS TALKS KNOWING SO MANY

00:03:09.382 --> 00:03:10.398
PEOPLE STILL NEED HELP

00:03:10.432 --> 00:03:11.435
INCLUDING AMERICAN BUSINESSES.

00:03:11.470 --> 00:03:13.487
HERE WAS HIS RESPONSE.

00:03:13.488 --> 00:03:15.665
&gt;&gt; President Trump: SHUTDOWN

00:03:15.666 --> 00:03:18.407
TALKS TWO DAYS AGO BECAUSE THEY

00:03:18.441 --> 00:03:20.055
AREN’T WORKING OUT.

00:03:20.056 --> 00:03:22.537
IT WASN’T THE WORKERS FAULT OR

00:03:22.571 --> 00:03:23.784
AIRLINES FAULT THAT CHINA DID

00:03:23.785 --> 00:03:24.267
THIS.

00:03:24.268 --> 00:03:25.683
&gt;&gt; Sandra: LARRY, YOU ARE

00:03:25.684 --> 00:03:26.829
ADVISING THE PRESIDENT.

00:03:26.864 --> 00:03:28.350
YOU SEE WHAT’S HAPPENING IN THE

00:03:28.384 --> 00:03:28.953
ECONOMY.

00:03:28.954 --> 00:03:31.249
CAN YOU TELL THE AMERICAN

00:03:31.284 --> 00:03:33.249
PEOPLE THAT SOMETHING GETS DONE

00:03:33.283 --> 00:03:34.257
BEFORE ELECTION DAY?

00:03:34.259 --> 00:03:35.288
DOES IT?

00:03:35.323 --> 00:03:38.177
&gt;&gt; I WOULD LIKE TO.

00:03:38.178 --> 00:03:41.720
I DON’T THINK THE RECOVERY

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.808
ITSELF DEPENDS ON THE SO-CALLED

00:03:43.842 --> 00:03:45.301
ASSISTANCE PACKAGE.

00:03:45.336 --> 00:03:47.265
HOWEVER IMPORTANTLY WE HAVE

00:03:47.266 --> 00:03:49.475
MADE TARGETED PLEAS FOR

00:03:49.476 --> 00:03:53.621
ASSISTANCE IN KEY AREAS AND NOW

00:03:53.623 --> 00:03:55.157
THE PRESIDENT BELIEVES WE

00:03:55.191 --> 00:03:57.689
SHOULD SHIFT INTO A STAND-ALONE

00:03:57.723 --> 00:03:59.399
BILL TO GET THE KEY POINTS

00:03:59.433 --> 00:04:00.052
THROUGH.

00:04:00.086 --> 00:04:03.234
THE BIG PACKAGE HAD WAY TOO

00:04:03.235 --> 00:04:04.717
MUCH SPENDING FOR STATE AND

00:04:04.718 --> 00:04:05.783
LOCAL BAIL-OUTS.

00:04:05.784 --> 00:04:08.540
ENDED THE HYDE AMENDMENT.

00:04:08.541 --> 00:04:10.125
FEDERAL FUNDING FOR ABORTION.

00:04:10.126 --> 00:04:10.971
ADDITIONAL HEALTHCARE FOR

00:04:10.972 --> 00:04:11.624
ILLEGAL IMMIGRANTS.

00:04:11.659 --> 00:04:13.423
A WHOLE BUNCH OF THINGS IN

00:04:13.458 --> 00:04:15.858
THERE THAT HAD NOTHING TO DO

00:04:15.859 --> 00:04:17.570
WITH COVID OR ECONOMIC RECOVERY.

00:04:17.572 --> 00:04:19.440
NOW WE’VE BEEN ASKING SECRETARY

00:04:19.442 --> 00:04:20.974
MNUCHIN DOING A GREAT JOB OF

00:04:20.975 --> 00:04:22.071
DIFFICULT NEGOTIATIONS.

00:04:22.105 --> 00:04:24.496
WE WOULD LIKE TO SEE SOME

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:25.291
UNEMPLOYMENT ASSISTANCE.

00:04:25.293 --> 00:04:27.817
WE HAD AN EXECUTIVE ORDER BUT

00:04:27.852 --> 00:04:29.432
THAT WON’T LAST FOREVER.

00:04:29.466 --> 00:04:31.072
WE NEED CONGRESS FOR

00:04:31.073 --> 00:04:32.060
UNEMPLOYMENT ASSISTANCE.

00:04:32.061 --> 00:04:34.531
LIKE TO EXTEND THE PPP SMALL

00:04:34.533 --> 00:04:35.842
BUSINESS LOANS.

00:04:35.843 --> 00:04:38.154
MONEY LEFT OVER, $135 BILLION.

00:04:38.155 --> 00:04:40.252
LET’S USE IT.

00:04:40.254 --> 00:04:42.598
THE PRESIDENT HAS SIGNED OFF ON

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:43.792
THE ASSISTANCE CHECKS.

00:04:43.793 --> 00:04:45.289
THEY WILL BE DIRECT MAIL.

00:04:45.291 --> 00:04:46.793
WE NEED LEGISLATION TO DO THAT.

00:04:46.828 --> 00:04:48.258
WE ALSO WANT TO HELP THE KIDS

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:50.814
GET BACK TO SCHOOL AND MAKE THE

00:04:50.849 --> 00:04:53.269
SCHOOLS AS SAFE AS POSSIBLE.

00:04:53.303 --> 00:04:55.671
NOW, THOSE ARE JUST VITAL

00:04:55.706 --> 00:04:57.546
TARGETED ASSISTANCE AREAS THAT

00:04:57.548 --> 00:04:59.808
WOULD STRENGTHEN THE ECONOMY,

00:04:59.809 --> 00:05:01.597
DEAL WITH COVID, AND HELP THOSE.

00:05:01.631 --> 00:05:02.650
YOU MENTIONED BEFORE CORRECTLY

00:05:02.684 --> 00:05:04.102
THERE IS A LOT OF FOLKS

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:05.076
UNEMPLOYED AND A LOT OF

00:05:05.111 --> 00:05:05.601
HARDSHIP.

00:05:05.603 --> 00:05:07.239
&gt;&gt; Sandra: THIS IS AN IMPORTANT

00:05:07.241 --> 00:05:07.707
ISSUE.

00:05:07.742 --> 00:05:09.741
&gt;&gt; LET’S HELP THEM IN A

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:10.530
TARGETED WAY.

00:05:10.564 --> 00:05:12.900
&gt;&gt; Sandra: I HAVE LIMITED TIME.

00:05:12.935 --> 00:05:15.199
WE WOULD LIKE TO SEE THIS ON

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:17.939
THE DEBATE STAGE.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.342
THE PRESIDENT SAID VIRTUAL NO

00:05:20.344 --> 00:05:21.282
THANK YOU.

00:05:21.283 --> 00:05:23.740
DO YOU THINK HE SHOULD STILL DO

00:05:23.742 --> 00:05:26.044
THE DEBATE EVEN IF IT’S VIRTUAL?

00:05:26.045 --> 00:05:28.247
&gt;&gt; I THINK YOU’LL SEE A

00:05:28.249 --> 00:05:29.312
RENEGOTIATION OF THAT.

00:05:29.313 --> 00:05:30.635
I THINK THE PRESIDENT IS

00:05:30.637 --> 00:05:31.706
GETTING WELL.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:34.160
HE WILL PASS THE TEST AND WILL

00:05:34.162 --> 00:05:35.606
BE SHOWING NEGATIVE TESTING, SO

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:36.839
I’M NOT SURE THAT’S GOING TO

00:05:36.841 --> 00:05:37.293
HAPPEN.

00:05:37.294 --> 00:05:40.934
I DO WANT TO SAY, SANDRA, IT IS

00:05:40.935 --> 00:05:42.355
SO IMPORTANT TO ME.

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:45.062
MIKE PENCE SHOWED LAST NIGHT IN

00:05:45.096 --> 00:05:48.837
THE DEBATE, WHICH HE WON GOING

00:05:48.839 --> 00:05:52.142
AWAY, IN A CALM MANNER HE TOOK

00:05:52.143 --> 00:05:54.797
COMMAND OF THE DEBATE AND

00:05:54.798 --> 00:05:57.655
CRUCIALLY TIME AND AGAIN

00:05:57.689 --> 00:06:00.996
POINTED OUT THE KEY DIFFERENCES

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:03.432
BETWEEN BIDEN-HARRIS AND

00:06:03.433 --> 00:06:06.046
TRUMP-PENCE ON TAXES, ON

00:06:06.081 --> 00:06:08.126
REGULATIONS, ON ENERGY, ON

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:09.170
SOCIALIZING AND NATIONALIZING

00:06:09.171 --> 00:06:09.863
HEALTHCARE.

00:06:09.864 --> 00:06:12.058
TOUGH ON CHINA AND GOOD TRADE

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:12.480
DEALS.

00:06:12.481 --> 00:06:15.293
AND, OF COURSE, RIGHT TO LIFE

00:06:15.327 --> 00:06:17.930
AND STACKING THE SUPREME COURT.

00:06:17.965 --> 00:06:20.202
HE MADE THIS SO CLEAR.

00:06:20.237 --> 00:06:22.285
DIFFERENCES MATTER, OKAY?

00:06:22.319 --> 00:06:24.757
YOU HAVE A VERY EXTREMIST

00:06:24.758 --> 00:06:26.666
LEFT-WING DEMOCRATIC CANDIDATE

00:06:26.668 --> 00:06:28.521
AND YOU’VE GOT A GOOD

00:06:28.522 --> 00:06:29.739
MAINSTREAM CONSERVATIVE

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.627
CANDIDATE WHO BY THE WAY

00:06:31.661 --> 00:06:32.867
INCREASED LIVING STANDARDS BY

00:06:32.901 --> 00:06:37.260
FIVE TIMES AS MUCH IN THREE

00:06:37.261 --> 00:06:40.090
YEARS AS THE  OBAMA PEOPLE DID

00:06:40.124 --> 00:06:41.128
IN EIGHT YEARS.

00:06:41.162 --> 00:06:43.774
I WANT HIM ON MESSAGE AND I

00:06:43.776 --> 00:06:45.442
WANT HIM TO SHOW THE

00:06:45.443 --> 00:06:47.380
DIFFERENCES BETWEEN THE TWO

00:06:47.414 --> 00:06:49.351
TEAMS AS MIKE PENCE DID

00:06:49.386 --> 00:06:50.417
BRILLIANTLY YESTERDAY.

